paper-poker-rules =
    {"["}head=2]TEXAS HOLD'EM[/head]
    (short version, the long one got lost at the factory)

    2 to 10 players. Everyone gets 2 cards face down. Nobody sees them but you.
    Take the joker out of the deck, hold'em doesn't use it.
    The player left of the dealer puts in the small blind, the next one puts in the big blind (twice the small one).
    Only two of you? Dealer puts in the small blind and goes first before the flop.

    {"["}bold]How a hand goes:[/bold]
    1. Everyone looks at their 2 cards. First round of betting.
    2. Flop. Dealer lays 3 cards face up on the table. Betting.
    3. Turn. One more card. Betting.
    4. River. Last card, 5 on the table total. Last round of betting.
    5. Whoever is left shows their cards. Best 5 out of your 2 + the 5 on the table wins.

    On your turn you can: fold (drop out), check (if nobody bet more than you), call (match the bet) or raise.
    Everyone folded but you? Take the pot, no need to show anything.

    {"["}bold]Hands, weakest to strongest:[/bold]
    - High card
    - Pair
    - Two pair
    - Three of a kind
    - Straight (5 in a row, any suit)
    - Flush (5 of one suit)
    - Full house (three + pair)
    - Four of a kind
    - Straight flush
    - Royal flush (10 J Q K A, one suit). If you got this, someone is probably cheating.

    Ace can be high or low (A 2 3 4 5 is a straight too).
    Same hand? Higher cards win. Totally equal? Split the pot.

    {"["}bold]Words you'll hear:[/bold]
    Pot - all the chips bet this hand.
    Dealer - the one dealing. Moves one seat clockwise after every hand.
    Blind - forced bet you make before seeing your cards.
    Fold - throw your cards away and sit the hand out. What you bet stays in the pot.
    Check - pass without betting. Only if nobody has bet more than you this round. That's why the big blind can check if nobody raised before the flop.
    Call - put in as much as the last bet.
    Raise - bet more. Everyone else has to match it or fold.
    All-in - bet everything you've got.
    Kicker - highest card that isn't part of your hand. Breaks ties when pairs are the same.
    Showdown - the end, when everyone still in shows their cards.

    Chips not included. Fights at the table are not covered by warranty.
    Nanotrasen reminds you: lost wages are non-refundable, won wages are taxable.
